# AdGuard Home ToolBox — release / Docker publish

Canonical repo: **ludditious/AdGuardHome-ToolBox**  
GHCR image: **ghcr.io/ludditious/adguardhome-toolbox:latest**  
CI: `.github/workflows/docker-publish.yml` (push to `main` or `workflow_dispatch`).

When the user asks for a **new build**, **publish**, **release**, **push to GitHub**, or **new container**:

1. Finish code changes; bump `APP_REVISION` in `web/app/version.py` when UI/docs/release notes change.
2. Commit on `main` (author: ludditious / `github.com@ludditious.com` when using `-c user.name` / `-c user.email`).
3. Publish from repo root: `.\scripts\publish-docker.ps1`  
   - Uses `LUDDITIOUS_GITHUB_PAT` or gitignored `Github-Access-Token.txt` (never commit tokens).
4. Confirm **Publish Docker image** succeeds on GitHub Actions; report commit hash and new `version.txt` after the bot commit.
5. All git author metadata and docs must use **ludditious** only.

`paths-ignore: version.txt` on push — after CI-only version bumps, run `publish-docker.ps1` to dispatch the workflow again if needed.
